Avoid odr-use of icu::AnnualTimeZoneRule::MAX_YEAR

ICU declares AnnualTimeZoneRule::MAX_YEAR as a `static const int32_t`
without `U_I18N_API` decoration. On macOS conda builds of ICU use
-fvisibility=hidden, so the symbol is not exported from
libicui18n.dylib. The macro INSTALL_STATIC_INT(AnnualTimeZoneRule,
MAX_YEAR) emits an odr-use of that symbol; at import time dyld then
fails with:

    ImportError: dlopen(...): symbol not found in flat namespace
    '__ZN6icu_7318AnnualTimeZoneRule8MAX_YEARE'

ICU defines this constant as 0x7FFFFFFF in tzrule.cpp. Inline the
literal value via INSTALL_ENUM to avoid the unresolved external
reference. The Python attribute AnnualTimeZoneRule.MAX_YEAR keeps its
original semantics and value.

--- a/timezone.cpp
+++ b/timezone.cpp
@@ -2128,5 +2128,5 @@
     INSTALL_STATIC_INT(SimpleTimeZone, STANDARD_TIME);
     INSTALL_STATIC_INT(SimpleTimeZone, UTC_TIME);
 
-    INSTALL_STATIC_INT(AnnualTimeZoneRule, MAX_YEAR);
+    INSTALL_ENUM(AnnualTimeZoneRule, "MAX_YEAR", 0x7FFFFFFF);
 }
